Revision history for Dist-Conformance

0.011 2026-11-26 TEODESIAN
    - A position of ~ puts a section of the overrides before every section, and conformance adopt keeps a section of its own that comes first there

0.010 2026-11-25 TEODESIAN
    - Add IniTemplate, which holds an INI file to its template with the overrides of the repository, and DistIni, which does so for dist.ini, authordeps included

0.009 2026-11-25 TEODESIAN
    - metamerge.yml declares aspell, which the spelling policy of the critic profile runs
    - The POD of each sub now gives the type of each argument, what it returns, how it fails, and an example call
    - Add the check AuthorDeps, which raises or adds each authordep of dist.ini that asks for less than its template

0.008 2026-11-24 TEODESIAN
    - A flavor can give SystemPackages a template metamerge.yml.  The check then fails unless the repository declares each dependency of the template, and the update adds the missing ones.
    - The update edits the text of an existing metamerge.yml, so its comments and the order of its keys stay as they were.

0.007 2026-11-20 TEODESIAN
    - The perlcritic profile is now the template with the overrides of the
      repository, and nothing else.  A repository declares each departure
      in .conformance.yml, under the overrides and the settings of
      CriticProfile: a parameter, a policy turned off, a policy of its
      own, or a global setting.  The check fails on every policy, parameter
      and setting that differs, and the update writes the template with the
      overrides.  Before, the check compared only which policies a profile
      named, so a new parameter in the template, a policy that the template
      turned off, and a hand edit of a profile never reached a check.  The
      comments of the profile are now those of the template.  The keys
      replace and retired are accepted and ignored: a policy that the
      template drops now leaves every profile without a list.
    - conformance adopt prints, as YAML, the configuration that makes the
      checks accept a checkout as it is now, such as the overrides that
      keep what a profile has of its own.  Merge it into .conformance.yml
      before the first update.
    - A module name in a flavor must be ASCII.  JSON::Validator compiled
      the old pattern outside the /a flag of the source file, so \w matched
      any Unicode letter.  A name such as Foo::Bär passed, and then failed
      with "does not load".  The pattern is now the rule of
      Module::Runtime, which spells out its character classes.  Such a name
      now fails with "is not the name of a module".

0.006 2026-11-17 TEODESIAN
    - The update of GitHooks installs each hook where git runs it from,
      as git rev-parse --git-path hooks says, so it honors
      core.hooksPath.  Before, it always wrote into the hooks directory of
      the common git directory, which git does not read when
      core.hooksPath is set.  So with a core.hooksPath of the tracked
      directory, such as git-hooks, the update installed a copy that
      nothing ran, and reported the install again whenever another
      worktree had installed different bytes.  Now it finds the hooks
      installed where they are tracked.  A checkout whose .git git cannot
      read is now an error of git, not a checkout without hooks.

0.005 2026-11-11 TEODESIAN
    - CriticProfile takes retired: a list of the policies that the
      standards have taken back.  The check fails a profile that still
      enables one, and names it, and the update removes its section, with
      its parameters and the comment directly above it.  Dropping a policy
      from the template could never take it away from a profile that had
      it, because a policy that the template lacks may be the
      distribution's own.  A template that enables a retired policy is an
      error.

0.004 2026-11-10 TEODESIAN
    - The update of CriticProfile appends to a profile that is there each
      policy of the template that it lacks, as the template writes its
      section, and leaves every line of the profile as it was.  It used to
      leave them for a person, unless replace: true overwrote the profile.
    - New check RefusedIniKeys: an INI file, such as dist.ini, sets no key
      that the flavor refuses for a plugin, such as user under
      [GithubMeta].  Unlike DataSchema, its update removes each such line,
      and nothing else.

0.003 2026-11-06 TEODESIAN
    - DataSchema reads an INI file, such as dist.ini, as a hash of its
      sections by their whole header.  A key that a section repeats is the
      list of its values, as Dist::Zilla reads it.  A file whose name ends in
      .ini is read so by default, and format: ini says it for any other.
      So a flavor can refuse a key of a plugin, such as user under
      [GithubMeta].
    - New check SystemPackages: a repository declares the packages of the
      operating system that it needs in metamerge.yml.  x_system_packages
      names each dependency, with its package for each packager, a package
      for a distro or a release of one, and a test that must run once it is
      installed.  x_system_sources holds the third-party archives of deb,
      each with the full fingerprint of its signing key.  The check refuses
      a name that is not a plain package name, such as a deb name that ends
      in -, which apt reads as a removal, a source that is not declared,
      and an archive that nothing installs from.
      Dist::Conformance::Check::SystemPackages->declared returns the
      validated declaration of a snapshot or a directory, and ->resolve
      what one host installs, and which dependencies it cannot resolve.
      conformance packages prints the packages, tests, sources or needs for
      the host of /etc/os-release, for a shell script, and exits 2 when a
      dependency has no package for the host.
    - Dist::Conformance::Schema::refuse dies with the message of validate,
      for an error that a schema cannot express.

0.002 2026-11-04 TEODESIAN
    - CriticProfile compares the policies of the profile with those of its
      template, and fails with the name of each policy that the template
      enables and the profile neither enables nor turns off with [-Name].
      Before, it compared only the first line, so a profile kept passing
      after its template gained a policy.  The keys header and outdated are
      deprecated and ignored; a flavor that names them still loads.

0.001 2026-11-02 TEODESIAN
    - Initial Release
